Freeze the four types Apple's Combine declares @frozen, and fix their boxes' layout

AnyPublisher, AnySubscriber, Subscribers.Demand and Subscribers.Completion are
@frozen in the iOS and macOS SDKs, so apps built against them lay them out and
inline their code: an AnyPublisher comes back in a register rather than through
an indirect result, and its PublisherBox is allocated by the app. Their stored
properties here match the SDK's (box; the four thunks and combineIdentifier;
rawValue; finished/failure), so freezing them gives the same layout. The box
classes behind them are @_fixed_layout in the SDK, with the same fields as here.

diff -ru a/AnyPublisher.swift b/AnyPublisher.swift
--- a/AnyPublisher.swift	2026-11-01 02:48:59.641786875 +0100
+++ b/AnyPublisher.swift	2026-11-01 02:49:31.604362230 +0100
@@ -62,6 +62,7 @@
 ///
 /// You can use OpenCombine’s `eraseToAnyPublisher()` operator to wrap a publisher with
 /// `AnyPublisher`.
+@frozen
 public struct AnyPublisher<Output, Failure: Error>
   : CustomStringConvertible,
     CustomPlaygroundDisplayConvertible
@@ -113,6 +114,7 @@
 /// A type-erasing base class. Its concrete subclass is generic over the underlying
 /// publisher.
 @usableFromInline
+@_fixed_layout
 internal class PublisherBoxBase<Output, Failure: Error>: Publisher {
 
     @inlinable
@@ -127,6 +129,7 @@
 }
 
 @usableFromInline
+@_fixed_layout
 internal final class PublisherBox<PublisherType: Publisher>
     : PublisherBoxBase<PublisherType.Output, PublisherType.Failure>
 {
